# Tech stack (Web Admin — S2)

- Next.js 15, App Router ONLY. No Pages Router, no `getServerSideProps`,
  no `getStaticProps`.
- React 19, functional components + hooks only. No class components.
- TypeScript 5.x, strict mode. `any` is banned — use `unknown` + a type
  guard, or a proper generic.
- Data layer: talks to the Express API (S3), not directly to Postgres, for
  writes. Read-heavy dashboard queries MAY use the Supabase JS client
  directly with row-level security — ask before assuming which, don't guess.
- Auth: Supabase email OTP session, verified server-side in middleware /
  route handlers. Never trust a role or gym_org_id sent from the client.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS. Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional
  classes. No styled-components, no CSS-in-JS libraries.
- State: server state via fetch in Server Components / route handlers +
  React Query (or SWR — pick one and stay consistent) for client-side
  mutations. No ad-hoc global state libraries without asking first.
- Forms: react-hook-form + zod for validation, mirrored on the API side.

## Banned outright
- `any`
- Pages Router APIs
- default exports for components (named exports only)
- inline `fetch` calls scattered through client components — go through a
  typed API client in `@/lib/api`
